# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your workflow code to write logs, report errors to your local notebook, and save partial work when a job is canceled. To read these outputs from your local notebook, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "I-set up ang code ng workflow mo para magsulat ng mga log, mag-ulat ng mga error sa local notebook mo, at mag-save ng bahagyang gawa kapag na-cancel ang job. Para basahin ang mga output na ito mula sa local notebook mo, tingnan ang [Magpatakbo ng managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| In the workflow | In your local notebook |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Write with a logger from the `logging` module, or call `print()`. | `job.logs()` returns the lines. |\n"
"| Raise an exception, or exit with a nonzero code. | `job.status()` returns `ERROR`, and `job.logs()` shows the traceback. |\n"
"| Call `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` and `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` return the code, message, and details. |\n"
"| Call `save_result()` in a `SIGTERM` handler. | `job.result()` returns the partial result of a canceled job. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sa workflow | Sa local notebook mo |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Magsulat gamit ang logger mula sa `logging` module, o tawagin ang `print()`. | Ibinabalik ng `job.logs()` ang mga linya. |\n"
"| Magtaas ng exception, o lumabas na may nonzero na code. | Ibinabalik ng `job.status()` ang `ERROR`, at ipinapakita ng `job.logs()` ang traceback. |\n"
"| Tawagin ang `send_error()`. | Ibinabalik ng `job.error_message()` at `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` ang code, mensahe, at mga detalye. |\n"
"| Tawagin ang `save_result()` sa isang `SIGTERM` handler. | Ibinabalik ng `job.result()` ang bahagyang resulta ng na-cancel na job. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs {#write-logs}"
msgstr "Magsulat ng mga log {#write-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. Read the logs with `job.logs()` while the job runs or after it ends.\n"
msgstr "Anumang isinusulat ng workflow sa standard output o standard error ay napupunta sa mga log ng job. Basahin ang mga log gamit ang `job.logs()` habang tumatakbo ang job o pagkatapos nitong matapos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up a logger {#set-up-a-logger}"
msgstr "Mag-set up ng logger {#set-up-a-logger}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the `logging` module from the Python standard library. `logging.basicConfig()` writes to standard error, which reaches the logs without delay. The format in the following example adds a timestamp to each line:\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang `logging` module mula sa Python standard library. Nagsusulat ang `logging.basicConfig()` sa standard error, na umaabot sa mga log nang walang pagkaantala. Ang format sa sumusunod na halimbawa ay nagdaragdag ng timestamp sa bawat linya:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`level=logging.WARNING` hides `INFO` messages from other packages, and `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` keeps `INFO` messages for your own logger. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` sets its own level with the `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable.\n"
msgstr "Itinatago ng `level=logging.WARNING` ang mga mensaheng `INFO` mula sa ibang mga package, at pinananatili ng `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` ang mga mensaheng `INFO` para sa sarili mong logger. Nagtatakda ang `qiskit_ibm_runtime` ng sarili nitong level gamit ang environment variable na `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`print()` also reaches the logs, but standard output is buffered, so printed lines might not appear until the job ends. If you use `print()`, pass `flush=True`.\n"
msgstr "Umaabot din sa mga log ang `print()`, pero naka-buffer ang standard output, kaya ang mga naka-print na linya ay maaaring hindi lumabas hanggang matapos ang job. Kung gagamit ka ng `print()`, ipasa ang `flush=True`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: get_logger() from qiskit_serverless adds a [PUBLIC] prefix that Functions uses to split provider and user logs for Catalog Functions; custom workflow logs strip it. Tested with 0.37.0: its lines have no timestamp, and logger.exception() and exc_info=True drop the traceback (PrefixFormatter builds new records with exc_info=None). Confirm whether to recommend the standard logging module for custom workflows, or to fix get_logger(). */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the log level for each run {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"
msgstr "Itakda ang log level para sa bawat run {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To debug one run without changing the code, pass the log level as an argument:\n"
msgstr "Para i-debug ang isang run nang hindi binabago ang code, ipasa ang log level bilang argument:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, set the level of your logger from the argument:\n"
msgstr "Para magawa ito, itakda ang level ng logger mo mula sa argument:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow has an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), declare `log_level` in it, for example as `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"
msgstr "Kung may [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema) ang workflow, ideklara rito ang `log_level`, halimbawa bilang `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: decide what to log {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"
msgstr "Best practice: magpasya kung ano ang ila-log {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Log enough to reconstruct a run from its logs:\n"
msgstr "Mag-log ng sapat para muling buuin ang isang run mula sa mga log nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**At the start, log what the run received.** Log the backend name, the number of circuits, and the other settings that change between runs.\n"
msgstr "**Sa simula, i-log kung ano ang natanggap ng run.** I-log ang pangalan ng backend, ang bilang ng mga circuit, at ang iba pang setting na nagbabago sa bawat run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log the start and end of each stage.** Use fixed messages that you can search for.\n"
msgstr "**I-log ang simula at wakas ng bawat yugto.** Gumamit ng mga nakapirming mensahe na mahahanap mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log iterations at a fixed interval.** For example, log a line such as `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` every 10 iterations, instead of every iteration.\n"
msgstr "**I-log ang mga iteration sa nakapirming pagitan.** Halimbawa, mag-log ng linya gaya ng `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` kada 10 iteration, sa halip na bawat iteration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log exceptions with `logger.exception()` inside an `except` block.** The line includes the full traceback, even if the workflow recovers from the error.\n"
msgstr "**I-log ang mga exception gamit ang `logger.exception()` sa loob ng `except` block.** Kasama sa linya ang buong traceback, kahit nakabawi ang workflow mula sa error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Turn off progress bars.** The logs store each refresh of a progress bar, such as one from `tqdm`, as a separate line. Pass `disable=True` to `tqdm`, or log at an interval instead.\n"
msgstr "**Patayin ang mga progress bar.** Iniimbak ng mga log ang bawat refresh ng progress bar, gaya ng mula sa `tqdm`, bilang hiwalay na linya. Ipasa ang `disable=True` sa `tqdm`, o mag-log sa isang pagitan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Keep the logs small.** Do not log large data, such as every shot. A managed workflow keeps only the newest 50 MB of logs for each job.\n"
msgstr "**Panatilihing maliit ang mga log.** Huwag mag-log ng malaking data, gaya ng bawat shot. Ang managed workflow ay nagpapanatili lang ng pinakabagong 50 MB ng mga log para sa bawat job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use the words \"error\" and \"exception\" only in messages about failures.** If a failed job did not [report its error](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include these words.\n"
msgstr "**Gamitin ang mga salitang \"error\" at \"exception\" sa mga mensahe lang tungkol sa mga pagkabigo.** Kung hindi [iniulat ng bigong job ang error nito](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), ang exception na itinataas ng `job.result()` ay naglalaman lang ng mga linya ng log na may mga salitang ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: report errors with send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send-error}"
msgstr "Best practice: mag-ulat ng mga error gamit ang send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status, and the traceback goes to the logs. A managed workflow does not store the error, even for a `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` returns `{}`, and the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include `error` or `exception`. Checks of argument types and ranges belong in an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), which rejects a bad run before the job starts.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nagtaas ng exception ang workflow, nagtatapos ang job na may status na `ERROR`, at napupunta sa mga log ang traceback. Hindi iniimbak ng managed workflow ang error, kahit para sa `ServerlessError`. Nagbabalik ang `job.error_message()` ng `{}`, at ang exception na itinataas ng `job.result()` ay naglalaman lang ng mga linya ng log na may `error` o `exception`. Ang mga pagsusuri sa type at saklaw ng argument ay nnnararapat sa [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), na tumatanggi sa maling run bago magsimula ang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report every error that stops the workflow with `send_error()`, so that your local notebook gets a short error with a code and details:\n"
msgstr "Iulat ang bawat error na nagpapahinto sa workflow gamit ang `send_error()`, para makakuha ang local notebook mo ng maikling error na may code at mga detalye:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` with the same text.\n"
msgstr "Nagtataas ang `job.result()` ng `QiskitServerlessException` na may parehong teksto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, raise `ServerlessError` where the error happens, and wrap the code of your entrypoint in a `try` block that sends any error with `send_error()`. A workflow adds this handler to Catalog Functions, but not to managed workflows:\n"
msgstr "Para magawa ito, magtaas ng `ServerlessError` kung saan nangyayari ang error, at balutin ang code ng entrypoint mo sa isang `try` block na nagpapadala ng anumang error gamit ang `send_error()`. Nagdaragdag ang workflow ng handler na ito sa Catalog Functions, pero hindi sa mga managed workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Raise the error again.** The final `raise` keeps the traceback in the logs and ends the job with the `ERROR` status.\n"
msgstr "**Itaas muli ang error.** Pinananatili ng huling `raise` ang traceback sa mga log at tinatapos ang job na may status na `ERROR`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Subclass `ServerlessError` to name a group of errors.** The handler sends the name of the class, such as `InputError`, as the `exception` field.\n"
msgstr "**Mag-subclass ng `ServerlessError` para pangalanan ang isang grupo ng mga error.** Ipinapadala ng handler ang pangalan ng class, gaya ng `InputError`, bilang field na `exception`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other exceptions also reach the handler.** They get the code `1`, and their `repr()` becomes the message, such as `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"
msgstr "**Umaabot din sa handler ang ibang mga exception.** Nakakakuha sila ng code na `1`, at ang `repr()` nila ang nagiging mensahe, gaya ng `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: custom (user) workflows run their entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py (fleets_runner.py _upload_custom_image_entrypoint). Only provider jobs get the main.tmpl handler, which calls send_error() for an uncaught exception. Should custom jobs get the same handler? Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0: a raised ServerlessError creates no ERROR event, and error_message() returns {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report a problem and continue {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"
msgstr "Mag-ulat ng problema at magpatuloy {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`send_error()` does not stop the workflow or change its status, so you can also report problems that the workflow recovers from, such as each circuit that it skips:\n"
msgstr "Hindi pinipigilan ng `send_error()` ang workflow o binabago ang status nito, kaya puwede mo ring i-report ang mga problemang nare-recover ng workflow, tulad ng bawat circuit na nilalaktawan nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns every error that the workflow reported, including the errors of a job that ended with the `DONE` status. See [Find the cause of an error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` ang bawat error na na-report ng workflow, kasama ang mga error ng job na natapos na may status na `DONE`. Tingnan ang [Hanapin ang sanhi ng error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pass numbers and strings in `args`.** `error_message()` shows only the first item of a list.\n"
msgstr "**Mag-pass ng mga numero at string sa `args`.** Ipinapakita lang ng `error_message()` ang unang item ng isang list.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Check the return value.** If a workflow cannot store the error, for example because the code runs outside a job, `send_error()` writes the error to the logs and returns `False`.\n"
msgstr "**Tingnan ang return value.** Kung hindi ma-store ng workflow ang error, halimbawa dahil tumatakbo ang code sa labas ng job, isinusulat ng `send_error()` ang error sa mga log at nagbabalik ng `False`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm which error codes user workflows should use. Catalog Function codes come from the IBM Quantum error code registry, which might not apply to user workflows. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up when a job is canceled {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"
msgstr "Maglinis kapag na-cancel ang job {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint, uploads the final logs, and shuts down the environment. Without a handler, Python stops immediately, and `finally` blocks do not run. The workflow also tries to cancel the QPU jobs and sessions that the workflow started with `get_runtime_service()`. See [Cancel linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Kapag nag-cancel ka ng job, nagpapadala ang workflow ng `SIGTERM` sa entrypoint mo, ina-upload ang mga huling log, at isinasara ang environment. Kung walang handler, agad na titigil ang Python, at hindi tatakbo ang mga `finally` block. Sinusubukan din ng workflow na i-cancel ang mga QPU job at session na sinimulan ng workflow gamit ang `get_runtime_service()`. Tingnan ang [I-cancel ang mga naka-link na QPU job](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep partial work, register a handler for `SIGTERM`. Your local notebook then gets the partial result from a canceled job:\n"
msgstr "Para mapanatili ang partial na gawa, mag-register ng handler para sa `SIGTERM`. Makakakuha na ang local notebook mo ng partial result mula sa na-cancel na job:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, add the handler at the start of your entrypoint:\n"
msgstr "Para i-enable ito, idagdag ang handler sa simula ng entrypoint mo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`sys.exit()` in the handler raises `SystemExit` in the code that is running, so `finally` blocks run before the script ends. The job still ends with the `CANCELED` status.\n"
msgstr "Nagtataas ang `sys.exit()` sa handler ng `SystemExit` sa code na tumatakbo, kaya tatakbo ang mga `finally` block bago matapos ang script. Natatapos pa rin ang job na may status na `CANCELED`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the handler short, because the workflow shuts down the environment soon after `SIGTERM`. For long runs, also save checkpoints, so that a later run can resume after a job fails or reaches the 24-hour limit. See [Best practice: checkpoint long jobs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Panatilihing maikli ang handler, dahil isinasara ng workflow ang environment pagkatapos ng `SIGTERM`. Para sa mahahabang run, mag-save din ng mga checkpoint, para makapag-resume ang susunod na run kapag nag-fail ang job o umabot sa 24-hour na limit. Tingnan ang [Best practice: mag-checkpoint ng mahahabang job](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm the time between SIGTERM and shutdown. The cancel is a Code Engine hard stop (fleets/handler.py cancel_job, cancel_processing_tasks=True), and the repo sets no grace period. Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0, the real fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py, and docker stop: the handler runs, save_result() writes the result, and result() on a CANCELED job returns it (the result endpoint does not check the status). Confirm on Fleets that a result written in the handler reaches storage before the hard stop. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to start a job and read its status, logs, and result.\n"
"- [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) to save checkpoints that a later run can resume from.\n"
"- [Choose a compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) to run your workflow with more CPU, memory, or GPU resources.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga rekomendasyon\">\n"
"- [Magpatakbo ng managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) para magsimula ng job at basahin ang status, mga log, at result nito.\n"
"- [Pamahalaan ang mga file sa iba't ibang run](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) para mag-save ng mga checkpoint na puwedeng ipagpatuloy ng susunod na run.\n"
"- [Pumili ng compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) para patakbuhin ang workflow mo gamit ang mas maraming CPU, memory, o GPU resource.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
